Node ID=52 she weighs you
Text=<A long pause.> Say I agree. You would walk north with my mark on you, into his country, and arrive. Why would you arrive? Tell me what you think is waiting, and I will know whether you have understood any of this.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=IN 7+
Reply Text=A relic is not loot. Somebody wants it whole, in one place, at one time -- and that is a ceremony, not a theft.
Go to node ID=56 she is satisfied
Icon=Attribute Icon

Requirement=CH 7+
Reply Text=Because I would rather owe you than bury you. That is worth more than rope.
Go to node ID=57 she almost smiles
Icon=Attribute Icon

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Because you have no one else left to send.
Go to node ID=58 she is done

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I will arrive. That is all I can promise you.
Go to node ID=50 her word
Is Default Reply=1

------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=53 her own orders
Text=<Her hand stops on the reliquary step.> You have a good ear. Say the rest of it, then, since you are counting my orders back to me. Who gave them.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=Outwit 10 greater or equal
Reply Text=Someone who wanted a crown and a witness, and sent a captain for both. You call him the Master. He has another name further east.
Go to node ID=56 she is satisfied
Icon=Attribute Icon

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Rome, at a guess. It is always Rome, under the paint.
Go to node ID=58 she is done

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Someone above you. That is as far as I need to count.
Go to node ID=50 her word
Is Default Reply=1

------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=54 the trade
Text=<She considers it the way she would consider a cart.> A word, then, and not a cargo. You carry what you are. Men stop a stranger on that road; they do not stop one of his. The price is that you keep walking and do not come back down it.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=And a share of whatever it is worth at the other end.
Go to node ID=58 she is done

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Agreed. A word for a road.
Go to node ID=50 her word
Is Default Reply=1

------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=55 the monk
Text=<Something goes out of her face.> He is still alive, then. I told them the cellar, and they heard the cellar. <She is quiet a moment.> Yes. We take them alive when there is room in the wagons. There was no room, and he could not walk, and that is the whole of why he is still in it.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Send me north, or the next people down there hear what you left him in.
Go to node ID=58 she is done

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Then make room for one more. Send me north.
Go to node ID=50 her word
Is Default Reply=1

------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=56 she is satisfied
Text=<She nods once, as though settling an account.> Then you will arrive. Go by the pass above Montaillou and do not take the valley road, whatever you are told in the village. There is an old man east of here who keeps a house of patient men, and the Crown is going to him, not to a church. Now take this before I remember what you cost me.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=<Take what she offers.>
Go to node ID=50 her word
Icon=Quest Icon
Is Default Reply=1

------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=57 she almost smiles
Text=<She almost smiles, and it does not reach anything.> Owe me, then. I have very little put by. <She rises, which she has not done since you came in.> You will not be stopped between here and the mountains. Past them I do not speak, and neither should you.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=<Take what she offers.>
Go to node ID=50 her word
Icon=Quest Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=58 she is done
Text=<She does not raise her voice.> No. I have heard what you are. <She turns her head very slightly toward the step, and the coiled things come awake.> Put him back in the cellar, or do not. I have stopped caring which.
Should Have Voiceover=0

